<title>USA: U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended Dec 27, compared with the Dec 20 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.18 vs 5.38</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............4.97 vs 4.88</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.61 vs 5.52</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.40 vs 5.39</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.50 vs 5.44</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.47 vs 5.46</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............6.58 vs 6.63</p>
</text>
